I found a CSS bug! In `style.css` line 42:
```css
a{color:var(--color-accent-text);text-decoration:none}
```
The variable `--color-accent-text` is not defined anywhere. It should be `--color-accent`. Let me verify this.

Looking at the CSS variables defined in `:root`:
```css
:root{
  --color-bg-light:#f8f9fa;
  --color-bg-dark:#212b36;
  --color-fg-light:#212b36;
  --color-fg-dark:#f8f9fa;
  --color-accent:#3b82f6;
  --color-accent-hover:#2563eb;
  --color-contrast:#334155;
  --color-reduced-motion:#e5e7eb;
}
```

Yes, `--color-accent-text` is NOT defined. It should be `--color-accent`. This is a bug.

Also in `main.js`, the copy button logic uses `btn.previousElementSibling` to get the code element, but the HTML doesn't actually have any `.copy-btn` elements in the `index.html`! The copy button logic is there but there are no copy buttons on the page. This is dead code or missing functionality.

Wait, actually looking at main.js more carefully, the copy button code looks for `.copy-btn` elements in the DOM. These don't exist in `index.html`, so that code never runs. But that's existing intended functionality that just isn't used yet - not really an "improvement opportunity" in the hardening sense.

Let me also look at what the `test_site.py` tests check for. The test `test_honesty_contract` checks for "http://localhost:8000/mcp" in the text. And the honesty contracts meta tags include this URL. This seems intentional.

OK, let me also check the `website/tests/test_design_system.py` - it doesn't test for `--color-accent-text`, so this CSS bug is not caught by tests. This is a real opportunity.

Let me also look at the `website/tests/test_make_og.py` and `website/tools/make_og.py` to see if there are issues there.

